    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "KM PROPERTY is delighted to present to the market No 12 Oakley Park. Set in a peaceful and sought-after enclave, just off Vernon Avenue this extended three-bedroom semi-detached property offers bright, well-proportioned accommodation throughout and provides an excellent balance of comfortable living space, privacy and outdoor enjoyment.\n\nViewing Video: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Gqt-ED_jBGE \nBehind the attractive red-brick façade the accommodation comprises of an entrance hallway with storage and guest WC. To the front there is access to two interconnecting reception rooms. This space offers a versatile space that can remain open for entertaining or closed off to create two separate spaces to relax and unwind. The extended kitchen/dining room also offers a furthers pace to entertain, it is flooded with natural light with the aid of three sky lights. The kitchen is fitted with arrange of wall and floor units. Integrated appliances include an oven, hob, extractor, dishwasher and washing machine. French doors lead from this space out to the secluded rear garden.\n\nUpstairs the landing area and stairwell is flooded with natural light with the aid of a side window. Three well-appointed bedrooms and an upgraded shower room complete the accommodation. \n\nOutside a large cobble lock driveway accommodates off street parking, a large flower bed is well stocked with mature shrubs. Side pedestrian access leads to the rear. The rear garden provides a tranquil setting to relax; it is laid in lawn and has two generous patio areas. A garden shed caters for further storage. \n\nThe unrivalled location is hard to beat as this wonderful home is located on one of Clontarf`s most sought-after locations. Located at just at the top of Vernon Avenue you are within minutes of all local shops, schools and Clontarf Promenade. St Anne`s Park is a short walk away. It the second largest municipal park in Dublin, is part of a former 202 hectares (500 acres) estate assembled by members of the Guinness family. The largest municipal park is also nearby (North) Bull Island. North Bull Island is an island located in Dublin Bay, about 5 km long and 800 m wide. It has been named by UNESCO as a biosphere reserve. It is the only biosphere reserve in a capital city in the world. The island, with a sandy beach known as Dollymount Strand runs its entire length, the island also hosts St Anne`s and Royal Dublin golf clubs. The area is also home to many sporting clubs with GAA, Rugby, Swimming, Sailing, Golf, Hockey and Tennis.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "HALLWAY - 1.71m (5'7\") x 5.43m (17'10\")\nFinished with wooden flooring the hallway has access to under stairs storage and a guest WC.\n\nRECEPTION ROOM ONE - 3.64m (11'11\") x 3.88m (12'9\")\nSet overlooking the front garden this well-appointed space offers an ideal space to relax and unwind. Glazed double doors lead through to the reception room two. Wooden flooring.\n\nRECEPTION ROOM TWO - 3.28m (10'9\") x 3.36m (11'0\")\nThis centrally located space opens through to the extended kitchen/dining room and opens via glazed double doors to the from reception space. It offers a variety of uses from a formal dining space or additional living space. A feature fireplace with gas inset fire creates a real focal point. This room is finished with wooden flooring.\n\nKITCHEN/DINING ROOM - 2.76m (9'1\") x 5.31m (17'5\")\nThe open plan, kitchen/dining space is flooded with natural light with the aid of large skylights and French doors and a large window. The kitchen is fitted with a range of wall and floor units. Integrated appliances. Include an oven hob extractor dishwasher and fridge freezer and washing machine. The space is finished with wooden flooring and opens directly out of the rear garden.\n\nBEDROOM ONE - 2.87m (9'5\") x 4.25m (13'11\")\nThis well appointed a double bedroom located to the front of the property and has built in wardrobes.\n\nBEDROOM TWO - 2.84m (9'4\") x 4m (13'1\")\nGenerous double bedroom located to the rear of the property.\n\nBEDROOM THREE - 2.24m (7'4\") x 3.32m (10'11\")\nThis well-appointed single bedroom is currently laid out as a home office. This bedroom has built-in storage and there is access from here to the attic via a pull down stairs.\n\nSHOWER ROOM - 1.62m (5'4\") x 1.79m (5'10\")\nThe upgraded shower room is fully tiled and is fitted with a wc, whb with built in storage and a large walk-in shower. A window allows for natural light and ventilation.\n\nNotice\nPlease note we have not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings, or services. Interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items. All measurements are approximate and photographs provided for guidance only."
      },
      {
